       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g a day. That is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g a day, and a single 5,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum. At that level there is a serious risk of acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day), which is within the 4 g/day limit. Many institutions cap it lower, at 3 g/day, for some patients.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and any note to add, such as PRN or a pain indication. I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 5,000 mg, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
