     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 5,000 mg three times daily (15 g a day) is in the range that causes acute liver injury and potentially fatal hepatotoxicity. A normal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. I can't think of a clinical situation where this dose would be intended.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Tell me which one and I'll enter it.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy.** A pharmacist can review the intended therapeutic goal with you and suggest an appropriate regimen.\n- **Review the clinical question.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or fever control, I can help you think through options to add or substitute, such as an NSAID, if appropriate, or a multimodal regimen.\n\nIf you think a dose this high is truly needed, please take it through your attending and pharmacy. They can then enter it through whatever process your institution requires for an exception. I won't enter it myself."
      }
